GREEN — implementation and targeted regressions
`digitization/native.py` now emits stable refusal reasons for missing/unreadable, malformed, encrypted, invalid-selection, and existing-output requests. It retains full adapter page inventory and feature coverage, marks unselected page scopes unexamined, removes their text observations, marks selected glyph coverage unexamined because native text cannot establish visual completeness, and records no-text pages as unexamined rather than blank. Any unsupported, approximated or unexamined feature makes the manifest/result partial (exit 2); extraction remains native-only. `inspect` validates pinned artifacts as before and reports selected/excluded/textless coverage, with a human-readable visual-completeness boundary.
The preexisting basic/layout success assertions were strengthened to partial/exit 2 because the native text layer alone does not establish complete visual coverage.

